01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
Pocketful of Miracles is a 1961 American comedy film, starring Glenn Ford and Bette
Davis, produced and directed by Frank Capra, filmed in Panavision.

11
01:23:06,666 --> 01:23:12,666
The screenplay by Hal Kanter and Harry Tugend was based on Robert Riskin's screenplay for the 1933 film Lady
for a Day, which was in turn adapted from the 1929 Damon Runyon short story "Madame La Gimp".

12
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
That original 1933 film was also directed by Capra—one of two films that he originally directed and
later remade, the other being Broadway Bill (1934) and its remake Riding High (1950).

13
01:38:13,333 --> 01:38:19,333
The film was the final project for both Capra and Thomas Mitchell.

14
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
It marked Ann-Margret's film debut.

15
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
Peter Falk was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor.

16
02:00:53,333 --> 02:00:59,333
The film explores themes of new york city,
prohibition era, gangster, deception, apple.

17
02:08:26,666 --> 02:08:32,666
